"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nFamous as the Harry Potter school, it attracts many visitors.  \n\nSeeing it in person, the sandstone buildings in Gothic Revival style lined up beautifully — the architecture was truly stunning.  \nModeled after Oxford and Cambridge, spires, arched colonnades, and medieval-style carvings blend throughout, giving the feeling of being somewhere in Europe.  \nIf I could enroll in a university like this, I think I would have studied much harder.  \n\nThere was a sign at the entrance asking for quiet, as it was exam season.  \nWe also moved as quietly as possible, exploring the buildings and taking plenty of photos.  \n\nWe stopped by the goods shop as well, where a stuffed toy that screamed 'university' caught our eye — we decided to splurge and bought it.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"